  "summary": "A Plenix action sheet on iOS keeps the system sheet’s structure and behavior: it rises from the bottom after the person starts an action, lists a few choices with destructive ones first and Cancel last, closes on a choice, a tap outside or Escape, and becomes a popover on iPad. The system confirmation dialog takes only a tint, so the full Plenix look draws the sheet as a bottom panel with the Plenix menu tokens: the overlay surface, the 8-point menu radius, rows 44 points tall with DM Sans at the body text role, hairline dividers and the danger content color for destructive choices. Apple’s default is a Liquid Glass panel of capsule buttons in SF Pro.",
